vinegar]]\n*2–3 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard]]\n*3 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n*1 cup [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n*1–2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoons]] [[Cookbook:Celery Seed|celery seed]]\n*3 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]]\n*¼ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Black Pepper|black pepper]]\n*¼ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Red Pepper|red pepper]]\n*1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]] flakes\n*[[Cookbook:Garlic|Garlic]] powder or [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]] garlic to taste (optional)\n\n==Procedure==\n# Combine all ingredients together and bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]]. Reduce heat and [[Cookbook:Simmer|simmer]] 10 to 15 minutes, until it thickens slightly.\n# Arrange [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]] pieces or [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]] chops in a greased [[Cookbook:Baking Dish|baking dish]].\n# Pour half of sauce over and [[Cookbook:Bake|bake]] at [[Cookbook:Oven_temperatures|350°F (175°C)]] for 30 to 40 minutes.\n# Pour remaining sauce over before serving.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* You can also keep sauce in refrigerator and use it like bottled BBQ sauce.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for barbecue sauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken breast]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery seed]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ketchup]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]\n[[Category:Recipes using prepared mustard]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Barbecue Sauce (Sweet)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 cup tomato catsup (ketchup)","sourceText":"1 cup tomato catsup (ketchup)","amountText":"1 cup tomato catsup (ketchup)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"¾ cup cider vinegar","sourceText":"¾ cup cider vinegar","amountText":"¾ cup cider vinegar